1-b0f8-459d-a6f3-7c50c2038591/e382f850-aad5-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w56ja.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l13w56j9/7d919a01-b0f8-459d-a6f3-7c50c2038591/e382f850-aad5-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w56ja.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>The total number of stereo isomers = 2<sup>n</sup> = 2<sup>2</sup> = 4, where n is the number of chiral centres.</p>\n<p>However, in bridge/bicycle compounds, the number of stereo-isomers is equal to the number of chiral centres because no carbon centres rotation is possible. Therefore, two stereoisomers would be possible for the given compound.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l13w918o/43682991-309b-44c0-b411-b927a39db62f/4ea8c790-aad6-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w918p.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l13w918o/43682991-309b-44c0-b411-b927a39db62f/4ea8c790-aad6-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w918p.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 25 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l13w918o/43682991-309b-44c0-b411-b927a39db62f/4ea8c790-aad6-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w918p.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l13w918o/43682991-309b-44c0-b411-b927a39db62f/4ea8c790-aad6-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w918p.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l13w918o/43682991-309b-44c0-b411-b927a39db62f/4ea8c790-aad6-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w918p.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l13w918o/43682991-309b-44c0-b411-b927a39db62f/4ea8c790-aad6-11ec-b70c-c9cdb7dbf989/file-1l13w918p.png?format=png 150